review:
While I can see the bones of the series in this game, like shooting grenades on enemies, stealth kills with an unsupressed sniper, timed schedule objectives that let you make a proper plan, I can't say this this is a worthwhile play for anything beyond "wanting to see where it all started".

The gameplay has aged not that well:
-Enemies detection is really unclear: sometimes they fail to notice anything, other times they are just agroed to you from the start of the mission, even when you're supposed to be in stealth;
-Movement is like playing on ice but every prop has super glue on it: touching any prop makes you stuck on it and needs you to back up to move again, regular movement is really slidy, especially if you don't cap your fps to 60 or below;
-Tutorials manage to be somehow overly plentyful yet explain nothing: I had no idea I had an inventory for the first mission and even when I did find it, I, at first, didn't know how to cycle through items, I still don't know how to scroll text on objective descriptions in the tab screen, covert kills are not well explained, because even when the game says I got a covert kill, everyone around (that didn't see the kill) are alerted from the sound, and lastly the first few missions are so annoying to play because your gameplay gets interupted by a short tutorial prompt every 5 steps;

And to wrap it up, this game is unplayable currently without a community fix. It is understandable for such an old game, but even with that mod I could not see the tutorial and final cutscene because it would break the game. Overall the game doesn't really show off anything impresive or important for the sniper elite series as it is now. Obviously it's important as the foundation still.

