Very nice for its time, though it has some bits that put it away from being better. Namely that:
1) Running has too much weight, so switching directions feels too slow;
2) Hostile machine gunners tend to be too accurate, easily taking you out from 50 m withou needing support to use a bipod (while you will always hipfire with it);
3) (Playing on the hardest AI) When in active combat, the enemies seem to be too aware of your position even after breaking line of sight. You can be out of sight after turning a corner and move 30 m away from it, and they will shoot at you right away after getting to said corner (as if they always knew where you were, even though you could have turned to a dozen of different spots while out of their vision).

With that said, still really enjoyed the game and would play again.
